SEG = "CAT"
CAT = "fnswCategories"
Q = [
    ("A lever action shotgun holds 7 rounds in its magazine. Which NSW licence category covers it?",
     "Category D", ["Category A", "Category B", "Category C"],
     "Section 8 of the Firearms Act 1996 puts lever action shotguns with a magazine of more than 5 rounds in category D. With 5 rounds or fewer the same shotgun is category B."),
    ("Under s 8 of the Firearms Act, a self-loading shotgun with a 4-round magazine falls in:",
     "Category C", ["Category A", "Category B", "Category D"],
     "Category C covers self-loading shotguns and pump action shotguns with a magazine capacity of no more than 5 rounds. Above 5 rounds they move to category D."),
    ("Under s 8 of the Firearms Act, a self-loading shotgun with an 8-round magazine falls in:",
     "Category D", ["Category A", "Category B", "Category C"],
     "Self-loading shotguns with a magazine of more than 5 rounds are category D, which is prohibited except for official purposes such as vertebrate pest animal control."),
    ("Which NSW licence category covers a blank fire starting pistol?",
     "Category H", ["Category A", "Category B", "Category D"],
     "Category H covers pistols, including blank fire pistols and air pistols. The Act's definition of firearm also includes blank fire firearms such as starting pistols."),
    ("Besides a genuine reason, what must a category B licence applicant show the Commissioner?",
     "A special need for category B", ["Five years as an A licensee", "A completed hunting season", "Membership of two clubs"],
     "Section 13 says a category B licence must not be issued unless the applicant also produces evidence of a special need to possess or use a category B firearm."),
    ("Apart from the special clay target licence, a category C licence needs the genuine reason of:",
     "Primary production", ["Sport/target shooting", "Firearms collection", "Recreational hunting"],
     "Section 14 limits category C to applicants whose genuine reason is primary production (or another reason the regulations prescribe), with a special need. Section 17A provides a separate clay target licence."),
    ("A category C applicant must show that their special need cannot be met by:",
     "Category A or B", ["A neighbour's rifle", "Category H", "A club's own firearm"],
     "Section 14(c) requires evidence that the special need cannot be met by any other means, including the authority of a category A or category B licence."),
    ("Unless a further special need is shown, a category C licence covers how many self-loading rimfire rifles?",
     "One", ["Two", "Three", "Five"],
     "Category C authorises no more than one registered self-loading rimfire rifle and one registered shotgun, unless a special need for more is established, for example a very large property."),
    ("Where may a category C licensee use their category C firearm?",
     "On their own farm land", ["On any rural land", "At any approved range", "In any state forest"],
     "Category C use is limited to primary production land owned or occupied by the licensee, or adjoining primary production land with the written permission of its owner or occupier."),
    ("A category D licence may be issued only for the genuine reason of:",
     "Vertebrate pest animal control", ["Primary production", "Sport/target shooting", "Recreational hunting/vermin control"],
     "Section 15 says the Commissioner must not issue a category D licence unless the genuine reason is vertebrate pest animal control and a special need is shown."),
    ("Which genuine reasons can support a category H (pistol) licence?",
     "Target shooting, work, collecting", ["Hunting, farming or collecting", "Self-defence, hunting or target shooting", "Pest control, farming or hunting"],
     "Section 16 allows category H only for sport/target shooting, business or employment, or firearms collection, plus a special need for a pistol. Personal protection is never a genuine reason."),
    ("A person's first category H (sport/target shooting) licence is issued as:",
     "A probationary pistol licence", ["A provisional rifle licence", "A minor's target permit", "A firearms collector licence"],
     "Section 16A says a category H (sport/target shooting) licence issued to someone who has never held one is a probationary pistol licence, which lasts 12 months."),
    ("For the first 6 months of a probationary pistol licence, the holder may possess or use a pistol only:",
     "At a pistol club, supervised", ["At home, in a locked gun safe", "On private rural land", "At any range, on their own"],
     "Section 16A(2) limits the first 6 months to the premises of a pistol shooting club under the supervision of a full category H (sport/target shooting) licence holder, while the club's safety course is completed."),
    ("A category H (sport/target shooting) licensee must not possess a pistol fitted with a magazine that holds more than:",
     "10 rounds", ["5 rounds", "15 rounds", "20 rounds"],
     "Section 51E makes it an offence for a category H (sport/target shooting) licensee to possess or use a pistol fitted with a magazine of more than 10 rounds."),
    ("Under s 4C of the Firearms Act, a pistol is a prohibited pistol if its calibre is more than:",
     ".38 inch", [".22 inch", ".32 inch", ".45 inch"],
     "Section 4C lists a pistol with a calibre of more than .38 inch as a prohibited pistol, unless it is a black powder pistol."),
    ("Under s 4C, a self-loading pistol is a prohibited pistol if its barrel is shorter than:",
     "120 mm", ["75 mm", "100 mm", "150 mm"],
     "Section 4C makes a self-loading pistol with a barrel length of less than 120 mm a prohibited pistol. For a revolver the figure is 100 mm."),
    ("Under s 4C, a revolver is a prohibited pistol if its barrel is shorter than:",
     "100 mm", ["75 mm", "120 mm", "150 mm"],
     "Section 4C makes a revolver with a barrel length of less than 100 mm a prohibited pistol. A self-loading pistol has the longer 120 mm limit."),
    ("Under Schedule 1, fitting a device that muffles the sound of firing makes a rifle:",
     "A prohibited firearm", ["A category B firearm", "A collector's firearm", "A category A firearm"],
     "Item 10 of Schedule 1 lists any firearm with an attached article or device capable of muffling, reducing or stopping the noise of firing as a prohibited firearm."),
    ("Which feature makes a rifle a prohibited firearm under Schedule 1?",
     "A folding or telescopic stock", ["A variable telescopic sight", "A sling and bipod", "A thick rubber recoil pad fitted"],
     "Item 11 of Schedule 1 covers firearms, other than pistols, fitted with a stock specially designed to be readily detachable or to fold, swivel or telescope. A telescopic sight is an ordinary accessory."),
    ("Which of these is listed as a prohibited firearm in Schedule 1?",
     "A firearm made like a pen", ["A double barrel shotgun", "A bolt action .22 rifle", "A single shot air rifle"],
     "Item 12 of Schedule 1 lists firearms made up in the form of a pen or pencil. Item 14 covers firearms disguised as other articles, such as a walking stick or key ring."),
    ("Which licence lets the holder possess firearms but never the ammunition for them?",
     "A firearms collector licence", ["A category A firearms licence", "A category D licence", "A firearms dealer licence"],
     "Section 9(3) says a firearms collector licence does not authorise possession of ammunition for any firearm in the collection."),
    ("A category A licence covers shotguns other than those with which actions?",
     "Pump, lever or self-loading", ["Break-open or side-by-side", "Bolt action or single shot", "Hinged or over-and-under"],
     "Section 8 puts shotguns in category A except pump action, lever action and self-loading shotguns, which fall in categories B, C or D depending on type and magazine size."),
    ("Unless the Act provides otherwise, a firearms collector licence excludes:",
     "Pistols made after 1946", ["Rifles made before 1900", "Muzzle-loading rifles", "Single shot shotguns"],
     "Section 8 excludes post-1946 pistols from the collector licence, except as the Act provides, for example under s 17C for members of an approved collectors' society."),
    ("A firearms dealer licence (other than for an armourer) authorises dealing only at:",
     "The premises in the licence", ["Any licensed gun show in NSW", "The dealer's own home", "Any approved range"],
     "Section 8 says a firearms dealer licence authorises its activities only at the premises specified in the licence, and s 18 requires those premises to be named on it."),
]
